          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c1_work_aws_santa_barbara_titled",
          "text": "This work, from AWS AI and UC Santa Barbara, is titled \"Automatic Clipping: Differentially Private Deep Learning Made Easier and Stronger.\" Differentially private training of deep networks relies on per-sample gradient clipping, but the clipping threshold R is a fragile hyperparameter that must be tuned carefully for good accuracy.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "work",
            "aws",
            "santa",
            "barbara",
            "titled",
            "automatic",
            "clipping",
            "differentially",
            "private",
            "deep"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s01_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s01_c2_authors_propose_automatic_clipping_d",
          "text": "The authors propose automatic clipping, a drop-in replacement that removes R entirely from any DP optimizer, so private training becomes as tuning-friendly as ordinary training while matching or beating the state of the art.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "authors",
            "propose",
            "automatic",
            "clipping",
            "drop-in",
            "replacement",
            "removes",
            "entirely",
            "any",
            "optimizer"
          ],
          "required": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "id": "problem",
      "heading": "Problem",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c1_differentially_private_deep_learning",
          "text": "In differentially private deep learning, every per-sample gradient is clipped to a fixed norm R before noise is added, and that single threshold R turns out to be decisive for accuracy.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "differentially",
            "private",
            "deep",
            "learning",
            "every",
            "per-sample",
            "gradient",
            "clipped",
            "fixed",
            "norm"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_picking_wrong_costly_imagenet_resnet",
          "text": "Picking it wrong is costly: on ImageNet, ResNet18 accuracy can collapse from forty-five percent to thirty-one percent when R is merely doubled.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "picking",
            "wrong",
            "costly",
            "imagenet",
            "resnet18",
            "accuracy",
            "collapse",
            "forty-five",
            "percent",
            "thirty-one"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_state_of_the_art_private_models_tend",
          "text": "State-of-the-art private models tend to need very small clipping thresholds that can only be found through careful, expensive tuning.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "state-of-the-art",
