          "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_crucially_best_thresholds_usually_sm",
          "text": "Crucially, the best thresholds are usually so small that nearly every per-sample gradient is clipped at every step, which hints that the precise value of R may not matter at all if we reformulate the clipping.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
